body:
Plan: `.pi/plans/2026-09-20-scripted-session/plan.md`

Modify: `src/lib.rs`

Extract the current post-selection tail of `open` into one private helper. It must preserve this order: validate checkout; list sessions; navigate immediately on canonical worktree metadata reuse; resolve layout; validate again; call existing `session_name`; call existing `Tmux::create`; navigate. The helper accepts an optional preset name: `None` uses `select_layout`; `Some(name)` performs exact lookup in `config.presets` and never invokes fzf. Return a clear `anyhow` error for an unknown preset only when creation is needed.

Add a public explicit-path entry point that calls the Git resolver from TODO-0001 and then the shared helper. Do not check `config.roots`, add request/config abstractions, change tmux metadata, or alter plain discovery.

Expected shape:
```rust
pub fn open_path(config: &Config, tmux: &Tmux, path: &Path, preset: Option<&str>) -> Result<()> {
    let checkout = git::checkout(path)?;
    open_checkout(config, tmux, &checkout, preset)
}

fn open_checkout(
    config: &Config,
    tmux: &Tmux,
    checkout: &Checkout,
    preset: Option<&str>,
) -> Result<()> {
    // validation -> reuse -> preset/picker -> validation -> create -> navigate
}
```

Reference: `src/lib.rs:235-306` — existing `open` selection and post-selection behavior. Reference: `src/lib.rs:196-218` — existing picker-based layout selection. Reference: `src/lib.rs:220-225` — metadata-based session lookup.

Add focused unit coverage where practical for exact preset lookup/error while keeping end-to-end picker/tmux assertions for the integration ticket. Preserve all existing tests.

Acceptance: ISC-3, ISC-4, ISC-5, ISC-6, ISC-7, ISC-12, ISC-A-1, and ISC-A-2 are represented in the shared control flow; `cargo test --lib` passes.

Dependencies: TODO-0001.
